---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { readBuildIntent } from "../site/build-intent";
import { isAnalyticsEnabled } from "../site/analytics-configuration";

const hasAnalytics = readBuildIntent() === "public" && isAnalyticsEnabled;
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Mythic China handles personal information and planned reader services."
>
  <article class="privacy-page page-shell" data-review-notice="privacy">
    <header class="privacy-hero section-space">
      <p class="section-context">Privacy Notice</p>
      <h1>Clear boundaries for reader information.</h1>
      <p>
        This notice distinguishes what is available now from services that are
        still planned and inactive.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-updated">
        Last updated <time datetime="2026-09-10">September 10, 2026</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-content section-space">
      <section id="controller" aria-labelledby="controller-heading">
        <h2 id="controller-heading">Controller and contact</h2>
        <p>
          Mythic China is a site brand operated by hyc. For this notice, hyc is
          the named data controller and is based in China.
        </p>
        <address>
          Privacy and data-rights contact:
          <span class="privacy-address">huyichen2019@gmail.com</span>
        </address>
        <p>
          Use the subject “Privacy request” for access, correction, deletion, or
          complaint requests. The address is plain text and does not create an
          automatic email action.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="current-state" aria-labelledby="current-state-heading">
        <h2 id="current-state-heading">Current services</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not currently accepting newsletter sign-ups and is not
          currently accepting Reader Requests. No newsletter or Reader Request
          form sends or stores information in this version.
        </p>
        <p>
          The only current contact route described here is a message that you
          independently choose to send to the public Gmail address above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact-data" aria-labelledby="contact-data-heading">
        <h2 id="contact-data-heading">Privacy-request correspondence</h2>
        <p>
          A message may include your email address, its contents, attachments
          you choose to send, and delivery metadata. We use it only to handle
          and document your request.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google provides the Gmail mailbox. Our operating rule is to retain the
          correspondence for 60 days after a request is closed, then delete it
          from the active mailbox and Trash, unless a longer retention period is
          required by law. Google’s underlying deletion and backup processes
          follow its own retention terms and may take longer; 60 days is not a
          supplier-level hard-deletion guarantee.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="newsletter" aria-labelledby="newsletter-heading">
        <h2 id="newsletter-heading">Planned Newsletter</h2>
        <p>
          If activated after separate account verification, the Newsletter will
          use Buttondown to process an email address for new stories and
          occasional editorial selections, no more than twice a month.
          Subscription will require email confirmation, every message will
          include an unsubscribe route, and open and click tracking will remain
          off before the first send and afterward.
        </p>
        <p>
          Buttondown is a United States provider, and its planned service domain
          is buttondown.com. No Buttondown account, exact action, subscriber
          record, or verified deletion workflow is active on this site. This
          notice will be updated before sign-ups open.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="reader-request" aria-labelledby="reader-request-heading">
        <h2 id="reader-request-heading">Planned Reader Request</h2>
        <p>
          If activated after separate form verification, the hosted Tally form
          will process the Entry page ID and required topic suggestion. An email
          address will be optional and will require separate consent used only
          to follow up about that suggestion; it will not subscribe the reader
          to the Newsletter.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tally creates a persistent Respondent ID in browser localStorage and
          may reuse it across forms in the same Tally workspace. That provider
          identifier will not become a Mythic China content ID, analytics
          property, or internal grouping key. Submission email notifications
          will remain off.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tally is a Belgian provider whose planned service domain is tally.so;
          its documentation states that form data is stored in Google Cloud
          Belgium. No exact hosted-form link or account is active here. Deleting
          submissions and Trash does not remove a Respondent ID already stored
          in a visitor’s browser; the account-level behavior and exit path must
          be verified before activation.
        </p>
        <p>
          The planned low-cost operating rule is to review submissions every 28
          days, delete records that are at least 60 days old, and empty Tally
          Trash in the same operation. When performed on time, this produces an
          expected retention window of about 60 to 88 days. The sole operator is
          hyc, with no independent backup; a missed operation can extend that
          period. Tally is not active on this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="analytics-hosting" aria-labelledby="analytics-heading">
        <h2 id="analytics-heading">Analytics and hosting</h2>
        {
          hasAnalytics ? (
            <p>
              GoatCounter is enabled on our public site. We use aggregate counts
              to understand which stories are read and improve the publication.
              Our basis is our legitimate interest in operating and improving
              this site. The service domain is mythic-china.goatcounter.com.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              GoatCounter is not enabled in this version, which sends no
              analytics requests. The public-site configuration uses
              mythic-china.goatcounter.com under the arrangements below.
            </p>
          )
        }
        <p>
          When enabled, analytics counts page loads, qualified readings, reading
          depth, and related-story link activations. These are counts, not
          identified readers. A reload counts again; returning to a page kept in
          the browser's back-forward cache does not start a new count. We send
          only the public page path and whether the count is an event; event
          paths include the event name and source article path. We exclude URL
          queries, fragments, referrers, email addresses, and form contents. We
          use no analytics cookies or persistent visitor identifiers.
        </p>
        <p>
          The provider still receives technical connection information,
          including an IP address, browser information, and the site's origin,
          and may process technical records to operate and protect its service.
          GoatCounter's operator is based in Ireland; its privacy policy lists
          hosting in Finland and Germany. See{" "}
          <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy"
            >GoatCounter's privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          The account is configured for 90 days of aggregate retention, with
          individual pageview details, sessions, referrers, browser and system
          statistics, screen size, location, and language collection disabled.
          Retention is applied through periodic cleanup, rather than guaranteed
          immediate deletion at exactly 90 days. The dashboard is private. The
          operator can export aggregates or remove site data; the provider says
          account-deletion backups may remain for up to 30 days. Aggregate
          counts do not let us identify or retrieve an individual reader's
          visits.
        </p>
        <p>
          To opt out, enable Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track in a browser
          that supports it. You can also load a page with <code
            >?analytics=off</code
          >
          or add <code>#analytics=off</code> to its address. This stops further analytics
          for that page, including after a back-forward restore; earlier counts are
          not removed. The address choice is not stored or carried to other pages.
          Browser privacy preferences apply across pages.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vercel is the selected hosting provider for Mythic China. When you
          visit a version hosted on Vercel, Vercel may process your IP address,
          approximate location derived from it, and technical system information
          to deliver, maintain, and protect the hosting service. For Vercel’s
          own privacy practices, see{" "}
          <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice"
            >Vercel’s Privacy Notice</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          This version does not accept newsletter sign-ups or Reader Requests.
          Hosting and security processing can still occur when you visit a
          hosted page without submitting information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        id="performance-monitoring"
        aria-labelledby="performance-monitoring-heading"
      >
        <h2 id="performance-monitoring-heading">
          Planned performance monitoring
        </h2>
        <p>
          Real user monitoring is not enabled. This version sends no performance
          measurements. We are preparing to measure loading speed, interaction
          delay, and layout shifts using a self-hosted copy of Google's
          web-vitals library and a dedicated Cloudflare receiver.
        </p>
        <p>
          The planned payload contains only a metric name, its value, a random
          identifier for that metric instance, and an update sequence. It does
          not contain page addresses, referrers, email addresses, or identifiers
          shared across visits. No cookies or browser storage are used.
          Cloudflare would still receive technical network information when
          handling a request.
        </p>
        <p>
          We plan to delete active measurements after 30 days and retain only
          aggregate results. Provider recovery and backup processes may take
          longer. The account, processing terms, request behavior, deletion
          process, and any required consent must be verified before activation.
          This notice will be updated with those verified arrangements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights" aria-labelledby="rights-heading">
        <h2 id="rights-heading">Your choices and complaints</h2>
        <p>
          Contact the address above to ask what personal information we hold, to
          request correction or deletion, to withdraw an optional follow-up
          consent, or to raise a privacy complaint. We may ask for only the
          information needed to verify and complete the request.
        </p>
        <p>
          This notice will be revised before any planned provider becomes active
          and again if the site adopts a custom domain or a different processor.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
